; F2a the bit fields INS / EXT (0F 31 / 39 INS, 0F 33 / 3B EXT; README "F2a"). The offset is the
; byte register of the ModR/M rm field, the width field w (a field of w + 1 bits) the byte
; register of the reg field (31 / 33) or the imm4 byte after the ModR/M byte (39 / 3B). EXT reads
; the word at DS0:IX (a prefix's segment) and, when the field crosses into the next word, the
; word at IX + 2, and leaves the field in AW; INS reads the word at DS1:IY (no prefix), inserts
; AW's low w + 1 bits at the offset and writes it back, then reads and writes the word at IY + 2
; when the field crosses. The crossing is decided on the registers whole (offset + width >= 16:
; the V20 suite's, funcref.py; the next word is read and written though no bit of the field
; lands in it); the offset register becomes (offset + w + 1) mod 16 and the pointer steps by 2
; when that sum reaches 16. The flags: none (F5: the V35 leaves the PSW, f5x; the V20 suite's
; byte subtract 15 - (offset + width) / + 1 was the core's until F5). (F5b: silicon, f5r insal) INS reads AW before it steps the offset register
; (an offset in AL or AH inserts AW's bits as they were); (F5b: f5r extal) EXT writes the offset
; register before AW (an offset in AL or AH is overwritten by the field).
;
; The machine: the field moves through the 32-bit pair {tmpc, tmpb} one bit a loop iteration
; (BFR / BFL, two words: the V35's iteration, as the shifts'), the loop counter loaded from
; SIGMA's low four bits (CN_SIG). EXT within one word: the word shifted left by the bits above
; the field (15 - offset - w) and right by the bits not in it (15 - w): silicon's 107 - 2o - 4w
; (docs/v35s-eu-timing.md "EXT and INS"); EXT crossing: the two words rotated right by the
; offset and masked (BFM): silicon's 61 + 2o. INS (bf_pass): the pair {0, the word} rotated
; right by the offset, the field merged (BFI), rotated on to sixteen rotations ({the word with
; the field, the field's spilled bits}): silicon's constant 94 within a word (92 at offset 0:
; the two words after the offset's rotations); crossing, the next word's low n bits replaced by
; the n spilled bits (the pair {the next word, the spill} rotated right by n, the next word
; rotated left by n: silicon's 4 a spilled bit, 128 + 4(o + w - 16)). The clocks around the
; loops with no act are OPEN words, each placed on the frozen model's clocks from the runs the
; README names (the setup before the read, the gaps between the bus cycles, the end).
;
; The read is posted first and its datum taken at once (F: the following clocks count from the
; read's end at every wait count); the imm4 form's setup ends with a fetch-free clock (fw: the
; frozen model's bf_read=fixed counts the read's setup on clocks no fetch runs). EXT's E carries
; wb (the frozen model's bf_ext wb 2: AW's write-back on past E, an OUT imm8 after it waits);
; INS's E on the fifth clock after its last write's post (held to the write's end: RAMEN). A memory
; ModR/M mode (no V20 form: the SingleStepTests have none) pops its displacement through the EA
; head and runs the register form on the rm field's byte register.

; ---- EXT (0F 33: the width in the reg field's byte register; 0F 3B: the imm4 byte), one body a
; form (the fixed clocks differ). The word's read is posted first (the frozen model's: the read
; after the ModR/M byte's take; the imm4 width byte taken while it waits), the field's
; arithmetic under it; the pointer's step on two of the end's clocks.

; (qprobe round 12-13, Q38 / Q44) the head of every form: `P . P . . C . . Y D` (the imm4 forms; the register-count forms one
; word shorter, `P . P . . C . Y D`): the ModR/M byte released on the third word, the commit word
; C, the word's read (Y, posted three words later), D. Then the field's two counted shifts at two
; words a bit (EXT: up by the bits above the field, down by the bits not in it, the second with
; a four-word entry skipped for a full-word field; INS: sixteen rotations), each structure's fixed
; words, and the end: EXT `PN .` (24 + 4 [n < 16] + 2 (16 - o - n) + 2 (16 - n) words after D),
; INS `Z G PN .` (70 + 2 [o > 0] - 8 [o + n = 16]). Across a word (o + n > 16, spec 9 B3): EXT
; 23 words, `U D` (the next word's read), 12 + 2 o + [n < 16] words ((r24) the [n < 16] word built in zz_late.uasm
; ext_xq / ext_xq2: a full-word field crossing skips it), `PN .`; INS 65 words, `Z D` (the first word written
; as a field ending at bit 15), 8 words, `U D`, 17 + 4 m words (m = o + n - 16), `Z G PN .`.

routine ext op=33 page=0f why="OPEN: (qprobe round 16, Q61 / Q62: the head `P . BP . C . Y D` (r,r) / `P . BP . C . . Y D` (r,imm4), replacing the round-12 head quoted below) silicon longer than the book (measured, the extra words OPEN): (qprobe round 12-13, Q38 / Q44) EXT reg8,reg8: the imm4 form's routine with the head one word shorter and no immediate (`P . P . C . Y D` ... `N .`; the qprobe ext runs, round 9)"
    pop=modrm eac=ext_r                 ; pop the ModR/M byte: register mode to the register form; a memory mode calls its EA head
    jmp=ext_r                           ; (a memory mode, returned from its EA head) the register form on the rm field's byte register
ext_r: open                             ; OPEN: (qprobe round 12-13, Q38 / Q44) a word with no act
    rl=1 bi                                 ; (qprobe round 16, Q61) B: bus-idle (waits while a fetch's pin cycle runs); P: the ModR/M byte released (the third word)
    open                                ; OPEN: (qprobe round 16, Q61) a word with no act (`P . BP . C . Y D`: one word fewer in front of C)
    bi alt                              ; C: the commit word
    ra=IX wid=WORD d1=ADDR s1=RA        ; the word's address IX
    rl=x bi                             ; Y: the request word (the read posted three words later)
    open call=w1                        ; OPEN: two words with no act (the call and the shared delay's 1)
    bus=MEMR seg=DSP                    ; post the word's read at IX (a prefix's segment, else DS0)
    f d1=TC s1=OPR                      ; D: F: tmpc <- the word
    ra=RM rb=REG wid=BYTE d1=TA s1=RB d2=TB s2=RA alu=ADD ax=RA ay=RB jmp=ext_c2 ; tmpa <- the width, tmpb <- the offset; SIGMA = offset + width; the common part

; (the register-count form's own copy of the body: its E word releases no immediate)
ext_c2: alu=BFK ax=SIG                   ; SIGMA = 15 - (offset + width): the bits above the field
    cnt=SIG alu=BFU ax=TB ay=TA jc=SGN:ext_x2 ; the counter <- the bits above the field; SIGMA = the offset's step (the new offset, the carry); crossing: the two-word path
    d1=ADDR s1=SIG d2=TB s2=TC alu=NOT ax=TA ; the address register <- the step; tmpb <- the word; SIGMA = ~width (low four bits: the bits not in the field)
    d1=TC s1=ZERO jc=CNTZ:ext_wr2        ; tmpc <- 0; no bit above the field: the second shift
ext_wl2: alu=BFL                         ; the word shifted up by one (tmpc's zero in)
    loop=ext_wl2                         ; the counter step (two words a bit)
ext_wr2: cnt=SIG d1=TC s1=ZERO           ; the counter <- 16 - n; tmpc <- 0
    jc=CNTZ:ext_wd2                      ; a full-word field: no second shift (its entry skipped)
    open call=w2                        ; OPEN: (qprobe round 12-13, Q38 / Q44) the second shift's four-word entry (the call and the shared delay's 2)
    open                                ; OPEN: (qprobe round 12-13, Q38 / Q44) the entry's fourth word
ext_wrl2: alu=BFR                        ; the word shifted down by one (tmpc's zero in)
    loop=ext_wrl2                        ; the counter step (two words a bit)
ext_wd2: open call=w11                   ; OPEN: (qprobe round 12-13, Q38 / Q44) twelve words with no act (the call and the shared delay's 11)
    alu=PASS ax=ADDR jmp=ext_t2          ; SIGMA = the offset's step
; the field crosses into the next word: the word at IX + 2 read too
ext_x2: alu=PASS ax=TB d1=TB s1=TC d2=TC s2=SIG ; tmpb <- the low word; tmpc <- the offset's step; SIGMA = the offset
    cnt=SIG ra=IX wid=WORD alu=INC2 ax=RA ; the counter <- the offset's low four bits; SIGMA = IX + 2
    d1=ADDR s1=SIG alu=PASS ax=TC       ; the address register <- IX + 2; SIGMA = the offset's step
    open call=w17                       ; OPEN: (qprobe round 12-13, Q38 / Q44) eighteen words with no act (the next read 29 clocks after the first at W = 0) (the call and the shared delay's 17)
    bus=MEMR seg=DSP wid=WORD           ; U: post the next word's read
    f d1=TC s1=OPR jc=CNTZ:ext_xm2       ; D: F: tmpc <- the high word; offset 0: the mask
ext_xr2: alu=BFR                         ; the pair rotated right by one
    loop=ext_xr2                         ; the counter step (two words a bit of the offset)
ext_xm2: alu=BFM jmp=ext_xq2             ; tmpb masked to the field's w + 1 bits (the whole word for a full-word field); (r24) the rest in zz_late.uasm (ext_xq2: no entry address moves)
    open                                ; OPEN: (r24) unused (the word kept so no address moves)
ext_t2: wr=RM wid=BYTE ws=SIG            ; the offset register <- the new offset
    wr=AW wid=WORD ws=TB jnc=SGN:ext_n2  ; (F5b: silicon, f5r extal) AW <- the field after the offset register; no carry: the pointer stays
    ra=IX wid=WORD alu=INC2 ax=RA       ; SIGMA = IX + 2 (the step on two of the end's clocks)
    wr=IX wid=WORD ws=SIG jmp=ext_e2     ; IX written
ext_n2: open call=w1                     ; OPEN: two words with no act (the pointer's two clocks) (the call and the shared delay's 1)
ext_e2: e ro                             ; E: pop the next opcode (N; the imm4 forms' P: the width byte, released here)

routine exti op=3B page=0f why="(qprobe round 21, spec 17 B, Q96) EXT r,imm4 is `P . BP . C . . Y DP . B` + (22 + v) words + `N .` (QPr20b e-exti, QPr16a ph-*-exti: the model +18, 0 lost): the imm4 released on the datum word, the second word behind it bus-idle, the length unchanged; OPEN: (qprobe round 16, Q61 / Q62: the head `P . BP . C . Y D` (r,r) / `P . BP . C . . Y D` (r,imm4), replacing the round-12 head quoted below) silicon longer than the book (measured, the extra words OPEN): (qprobe round 12-13, Q38 / Q44) EXT reg8,imm4 (the qprobe exti runs, r12b / r13a): the head, the two counted shifts, `PN .`; across a word the next word's read and the offset's rotation"
    pop=modrm eac=exti_r                ; pop the ModR/M byte: register mode to the register form; a memory mode calls its EA head
    jmp=exti_r                          ; (a memory mode, returned from its EA head) the register form on the rm field's byte register
exti_r: open                            ; OPEN: (qprobe round 12-13, Q38 / Q44) a word with no act
    rl=1 bi                                 ; (qprobe round 16, Q61) B: bus-idle (waits while a fetch's pin cycle runs); P: the ModR/M byte released (the third word)
    pop=il                              ; pop the imm4 width byte (released on the E word)
    bi alt                              ; C: the commit word
    open                                ; OPEN: a word with no act
    ra=IX wid=WORD d1=ADDR s1=RA        ; the word's address IX
    rl=x bi                             ; Y: the request word (the read posted three words later)
    open call=w1                        ; OPEN: two words with no act (the call and the shared delay's 1)
    bus=MEMR seg=DSP                    ; post the word's read at IX (a prefix's segment, else DS0)
    f d1=TC s1=OPR rl=1                 ; D: F: tmpc <- the word; (qprobe round 21, spec 17 B, Q96) P: the imm4 width byte released on the datum word
    ra=RM wid=BYTE d1=TA s1=IMM8 d2=TB s2=RA alu=ADD ax=RA ay=IMM8 ; tmpa <- the width, tmpb <- the offset; SIGMA = offset + width
ext_c: alu=BFK ax=SIG bi                ; SIGMA = 15 - (offset + width): the bits above the field; (qprobe round 21, Q96) B: the second word behind the datum word bus-idle
    cnt=SIG alu=BFU ax=TB ay=TA jc=SGN:ext_x ; the counter <- the bits above the field; SIGMA = the offset's step (the new offset, the carry); crossing: the two-word path
    d1=ADDR s1=SIG d2=TB s2=TC alu=NOT ax=TA ; the address register <- the step; tmpb <- the word; SIGMA = ~width (low four bits: the bits not in the field)
    d1=TC s1=ZERO jc=CNTZ:ext_wr        ; tmpc <- 0; no bit above the field: the second shift
ext_wl: alu=BFL                         ; the word shifted up by one (tmpc's zero in)
    loop=ext_wl                         ; the counter step (two words a bit)
ext_wr: cnt=SIG d1=TC s1=ZERO           ; the counter <- 16 - n; tmpc <- 0
    jc=CNTZ:ext_wd                      ; a full-word field: no second shift (its entry skipped)
    open call=w2                        ; OPEN: (qprobe round 12-13, Q38 / Q44) the second shift's four-word entry (the call and the shared delay's 2)
    open                                ; OPEN: (qprobe round 12-13, Q38 / Q44) the entry's fourth word
ext_wrl: alu=BFR                        ; the word shifted down by one (tmpc's zero in)
    loop=ext_wrl                        ; the counter step (two words a bit)
ext_wd: open call=w11                   ; OPEN: (qprobe round 12-13, Q38 / Q44) twelve words with no act (the call and the shared delay's 11)
    alu=PASS ax=ADDR jmp=ext_t          ; SIGMA = the offset's step
; the field crosses into the next word: the word at IX + 2 read too
ext_x: alu=PASS ax=TB d1=TB s1=TC d2=TC s2=SIG ; tmpb <- the low word; tmpc <- the offset's step; SIGMA = the offset
    cnt=SIG ra=IX wid=WORD alu=INC2 ax=RA ; the counter <- the offset's low four bits; SIGMA = IX + 2
    d1=ADDR s1=SIG alu=PASS ax=TC       ; the address register <- IX + 2; SIGMA = the offset's step
    open call=w17                       ; OPEN: (qprobe round 12-13, Q38 / Q44) eighteen words with no act (the next read 29 clocks after the first at W = 0) (the call and the shared delay's 17)
    bus=MEMR seg=DSP wid=WORD           ; U: post the next word's read
    f d1=TC s1=OPR jc=CNTZ:ext_xm       ; D: F: tmpc <- the high word; offset 0: the mask
ext_xr: alu=BFR                         ; the pair rotated right by one
    loop=ext_xr                         ; the counter step (two words a bit of the offset)
ext_xm: alu=BFM jmp=ext_xq             ; tmpb masked to the field's w + 1 bits (the whole word for a full-word field); (r24) the rest in zz_late.uasm (ext_xq: no entry address moves)
    open                                ; OPEN: (r24) unused (the word kept so no address moves)
ext_t: wr=RM wid=BYTE ws=SIG            ; the offset register <- the new offset
    wr=AW wid=WORD ws=TB jnc=SGN:ext_n  ; (F5b: silicon, f5r extal) AW <- the field after the offset register; no carry: the pointer stays
    ra=IX wid=WORD alu=INC2 ax=RA       ; SIGMA = IX + 2 (the step on two of the end's clocks)
    wr=IX wid=WORD ws=SIG jmp=ext_e     ; IX written
ext_n: open call=w1                     ; OPEN: two words with no act (the pointer's two clocks) (the call and the shared delay's 1)
ext_e: e ro                             ; E: N (qprobe round 21, Q96: the width byte released on the datum word)

routine ins op=31 page=0f why="OPEN: (qprobe round 16, Q61 / Q62: the head `P . BP . C . Y D` (r,r) / `P . BP . C . . Y D` (r,imm4), replacing the round-12 head quoted below) silicon longer than the book (measured, the extra words OPEN): (qprobe round 12-13, Q38 / Q44) INS reg8,reg8: the imm4 form's routine with the head one word shorter and no immediate (`Z G N .`; the qprobe ins runs, round 9)"
    pop=modrm eac=ins_r                 ; pop the ModR/M byte: register mode to the register form; a memory mode calls its EA head
    jmp=ins_r                           ; (a memory mode, returned from its EA head) the register form on the rm field's byte register
ins_r: open                             ; OPEN: (qprobe round 12-13, Q38 / Q44) a word with no act
    rl=1 bi                                 ; (qprobe round 16, Q61) B: bus-idle (waits while a fetch's pin cycle runs); P: the ModR/M byte released (the third word)
    open                                ; OPEN: (qprobe round 16, Q61) a word with no act (`P . BP . C . Y D`: one word fewer in front of C)
    bi alt                              ; C: the commit word
    ra=IY wid=WORD d1=ADDR s1=RA        ; the word's address IY
    rl=x bi                             ; Y: the request word (the read posted three words later)
    open call=w1                        ; OPEN: two words with no act (the call and the shared delay's 1)
    bus=MEMR seg=DS1                    ; post the word's read at DS1:IY (no prefix)
    f d1=TC s1=OPR                      ; D: F: tmpc <- the word
    ra=RM rb=REG wid=BYTE d1=TA s1=RB d2=TB s2=RA alu=ADD ax=RA ay=RB jmp=ins_c2 ; tmpa <- the width, tmpb <- the offset; SIGMA = offset + width; the common part

; (the register-count form's own copy of the body: its E word releases no immediate)
ins_c2: alu=INC ax=SIG                   ; SIGMA = offset + width + 1
    alu=BFK ax=SIG                      ; SIGMA = 14 - (offset + width); no flags
    alu=INC ax=SIG                      ; SIGMA = 15 - (offset + width): its sign the crossing
    alu=BFU ax=TB ay=TA jc=SGN:ins_x2    ; SIGMA = the offset's step; crossing: the two-word path
    call=bf_pass                        ; the insertion into the word (tmpc)
    alu=PASS ax=ADDR                    ; SIGMA = the offset's step
    jnc=SGN:ins_n2                       ; the field ends below bit 15: the long path
    open call=w17                       ; OPEN: eighteen words with no act (the field ending at bit 15: eight words fewer) (the call and the shared delay's 17)
    ra=IY wid=WORD d1=ADDR s1=RA d2=OPRW s2=TC alu=INC2 ax=RA ; Z's word: the address register <- IY; the write datum <- the word; SIGMA = IY + 2
    bus=MEMW seg=DS1 wid=WORD wr=IY ws=SIG jmp=ins_e2 ; Z: post the word's write; IY written (the field ended at bit 15)
ins_n2: open call=w24                    ; OPEN: twenty-five words with no act (the call and the shared delay's 24)
    open                                ; OPEN: a word with no act
    ra=IY wid=WORD d1=ADDR s1=RA d2=OPRW s2=TC ; Z's word: the address register <- IY; the write datum <- the word
    bus=MEMW seg=DS1 wid=WORD           ; Z: post the word's write
ins_e2: e ro bi                          ; E: G N (the imm4 forms' P: the width byte); held until the write's end (RAMEN)
; the field crosses into the next word: the word at IY + 2 read and written
ins_x2: call=bf_pass                     ; the insertion into the low word (tmpc); tmpb <- the spilled bits
    open call=w20                       ; OPEN: twenty-one words with no act (the call and the shared delay's 20)
    ra=IY wid=WORD d1=ADDR s1=RA d2=OPRW s2=TC alu=PASS ax=ADDR ; Z's word: the address register <- IY; the write datum <- the low word; SIGMA = the offset's step
    ra=IY wid=WORD d1=TC s1=SIG alu=INC2 ax=RA bus=MEMW seg=DS1 ; Z: post the low word's write; tmpc <- the step; SIGMA = IY + 2
    f d1=ADDR s1=SIG alu=PASS ax=TC     ; D: F: the low word's write's end; the address register <- IY + 2; SIGMA = the offset's step
    open call=w8                        ; OPEN: nine words with no act (the call and the shared delay's 8)
    bus=MEMR seg=DS1 wid=WORD           ; U: post the next word's read
    f d1=TC s1=OPR jnc=SGN:ins_xw2       ; D: F: tmpc <- the high word; no carry: no bit spilled
    cnt=SIG                             ; the counter <- the spilled bits m
    jc=CNTZ:ins_xw2                      ; none
ins_xr2: alu=BFR                         ; the pair {the high word, the spill} rotated right by one
    loop=ins_xr2                         ; the counter step
    cnt=SIG d1=TB s1=TC                 ; the counter <- m; tmpb <- tmpc (the high word rotated alone)
ins_xl2: alu=BFL                         ; the high word rotated left by one
    loop=ins_xl2                         ; the counter step
ins_xw2: open jnc=SGN:ins_xs2             ; OPEN: a word with no act; no carry: the pointer stays
    ra=IY wid=WORD alu=INC2 ax=RA       ; SIGMA = IY + 2
    wr=IY wid=WORD ws=SIG               ; IY written
    open call=w9                        ; OPEN: ten words with no act (the call and the shared delay's 9)
    open jmp=ins_xo2                     ; OPEN: a word with no act
ins_xs2: open call=w11                   ; OPEN: twelve words with no act (the call and the shared delay's 11)
    open                                ; OPEN: a word with no act
ins_xo2: d1=OPRW s1=TC                   ; Z's word: the write datum <- the high word
    bus=MEMW seg=DS1 wid=WORD jmp=ins_e2 ; Z: post the high word's write

routine insi op=39 page=0f why="(qprobe round 21, spec 17 B, Q96) INS r,imm4 is `P . BP . C . . Y DP . . B` + (67 + v) words + `Z G N .` (QPr20b e-insi: the model +11, 0 lost): the imm4 released on the datum word, the third word behind it bus-idle; OPEN: (qprobe round 16, Q61 / Q62: the head `P . BP . C . Y D` (r,r) / `P . BP . C . . Y D` (r,imm4), replacing the round-12 head quoted below) silicon longer than the book (measured, the extra words OPEN): (qprobe round 12-13, Q38 / Q44) INS reg8,imm4 (the qprobe insi runs, r12b / r13a): the head, the sixteen rotations, `Z G PN .`; across a word the first word written, the next read and written"
    pop=modrm eac=insi_r                ; pop the ModR/M byte: register mode to the register form; a memory mode calls its EA head
    jmp=insi_r                          ; (a memory mode, returned from its EA head) the register form on the rm field's byte register
insi_r: open                            ; OPEN: (qprobe round 12-13, Q38 / Q44) a word with no act
    rl=1 bi                                 ; (qprobe round 16, Q61) B: bus-idle (waits while a fetch's pin cycle runs); P: the ModR/M byte released (the third word)
    pop=il                              ; pop the imm4 width byte (released on the E word)
    bi alt                              ; C: the commit word
    open                                ; OPEN: a word with no act
    ra=IY wid=WORD d1=ADDR s1=RA        ; the word's address IY
    rl=x bi                             ; Y: the request word (the read posted three words later)
    open call=w1                        ; OPEN: two words with no act (the call and the shared delay's 1)
    bus=MEMR seg=DS1                    ; post the word's read at DS1:IY (no prefix)
    f d1=TC s1=OPR rl=1                 ; D: F: tmpc <- the word; (qprobe round 21, spec 17 B, Q96) P: the imm4 width byte released on the datum word
    ra=RM wid=BYTE d1=TA s1=IMM8 d2=TB s2=RA alu=ADD ax=RA ay=IMM8 ; tmpa <- the width, tmpb <- the offset; SIGMA = offset + width
ins_c: alu=INC ax=SIG                   ; SIGMA = offset + width + 1
    alu=BFK ax=SIG bi                   ; SIGMA = 14 - (offset + width); no flags; (qprobe round 21, Q96) B: the third word behind the datum word bus-idle
    alu=INC ax=SIG                      ; SIGMA = 15 - (offset + width): its sign the crossing
    alu=BFU ax=TB ay=TA jc=SGN:ins_x    ; SIGMA = the offset's step; crossing: the two-word path
    call=bf_pass                        ; the insertion into the word (tmpc)
    alu=PASS ax=ADDR                    ; SIGMA = the offset's step
    jnc=SGN:ins_n                       ; the field ends below bit 15: the long path
    open call=w17                       ; OPEN: eighteen words with no act (the field ending at bit 15: eight words fewer) (the call and the shared delay's 17)
    ra=IY wid=WORD d1=ADDR s1=RA d2=OPRW s2=TC alu=INC2 ax=RA ; Z's word: the address register <- IY; the write datum <- the word; SIGMA = IY + 2
    bus=MEMW seg=DS1 wid=WORD wr=IY ws=SIG jmp=ins_e ; Z: post the word's write; IY written (the field ended at bit 15)
ins_n: open call=w24                    ; OPEN: twenty-five words with no act (the call and the shared delay's 24)
    open                                ; OPEN: a word with no act
    ra=IY wid=WORD d1=ADDR s1=RA d2=OPRW s2=TC ; Z's word: the address register <- IY; the write datum <- the word
    bus=MEMW seg=DS1 wid=WORD           ; Z: post the word's write
ins_e: e ro bi                          ; E: G N (qprobe round 21, Q96: the width byte released on the datum word); held until the write's end (RAMEN)
; the field crosses into the next word: the word at IY + 2 read and written
ins_x: call=bf_pass                     ; the insertion into the low word (tmpc); tmpb <- the spilled bits
    open call=w20                       ; OPEN: twenty-one words with no act (the call and the shared delay's 20)
    ra=IY wid=WORD d1=ADDR s1=RA d2=OPRW s2=TC alu=PASS ax=ADDR ; Z's word: the address register <- IY; the write datum <- the low word; SIGMA = the offset's step
    ra=IY wid=WORD d1=TC s1=SIG alu=INC2 ax=RA bus=MEMW seg=DS1 ; Z: post the low word's write; tmpc <- the step; SIGMA = IY + 2
    f d1=ADDR s1=SIG alu=PASS ax=TC     ; D: F: the low word's write's end; the address register <- IY + 2; SIGMA = the offset's step
    open call=w8                        ; OPEN: nine words with no act (the call and the shared delay's 8)
    bus=MEMR seg=DS1 wid=WORD           ; U: post the next word's read
    f d1=TC s1=OPR jnc=SGN:ins_xw       ; D: F: tmpc <- the high word; no carry: no bit spilled
    cnt=SIG                             ; the counter <- the spilled bits m
    jc=CNTZ:ins_xw                      ; none
ins_xr: alu=BFR                         ; the pair {the high word, the spill} rotated right by one
    loop=ins_xr                         ; the counter step
    cnt=SIG d1=TB s1=TC                 ; the counter <- m; tmpb <- tmpc (the high word rotated alone)
ins_xl: alu=BFL                         ; the high word rotated left by one
    loop=ins_xl                         ; the counter step
ins_xw: open jnc=SGN:ins_xs             ; OPEN: a word with no act; no carry: the pointer stays
    ra=IY wid=WORD alu=INC2 ax=RA       ; SIGMA = IY + 2
    wr=IY wid=WORD ws=SIG               ; IY written
    open call=w9                        ; OPEN: ten words with no act (the call and the shared delay's 9)
    open jmp=ins_xo                     ; OPEN: a word with no act
ins_xs: open call=w11                   ; OPEN: twelve words with no act (the call and the shared delay's 11)
    open                                ; OPEN: a word with no act
ins_xo: d1=OPRW s1=TC                   ; Z's word: the write datum <- the high word
    bus=MEMW seg=DS1 wid=WORD jmp=ins_e ; Z: post the high word's write

; the insertion pass (INS, called): SIGMA the offset's step, tmpb the offset, tmpa the width,
; tmpc the word. (F5b) The offset register is written on the last word, after AW is read.
routine bf_pass why="OPEN: the INS insertion pass (called by ins / insi): the two words after the offset rotations are OPEN (silicon 92 at offset 0 against 94)"
    d1=ADDR s1=SIG alu=PASS ax=TB       ; the address register <- the step; SIGMA = the offset
    cnt=SIG alu=NOT ax=TB d1=TB s1=TC d2=TC s2=ZERO; the counter <- the offset's low four bits; SIGMA = ~offset; tmpb <- the word; tmpc <- 0
    jc=CNTZ:bfp_m                       ; offset 0: the merge
bfp_r: alu=BFR                          ; the pair rotated right by one
    loop=bfp_r                          ; the counter step
    open                                ; OPEN: a clock with no act after the offset's rotations (INS 94, 92 at offset 0)
    open                                ; OPEN: a clock with no act after the offset's rotations (INS 94, 92 at offset 0)
bfp_m: ra=AW wid=WORD alu=BFI ax=RA cnt=SIG; AW's low w + 1 bits into tmpb; the counter <- 15 - offset
    jc=CNTZ:bfp_l                       ; none: the last rotation
bfp_s: alu=BFR                          ; the pair rotated right by one
    loop=bfp_s                          ; the counter step
bfp_l: alu=BFR wr=RM wid=BYTE ws=ADDR ret ; the sixteenth rotation; (F5b) the offset register <- the step (after AW is read: an offset in AL / AH inserts AW's bits as they were, f5r insal); return
